.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt RACH2-GAME 1
.Os Rach2
.Sh NAME
.Nm rach2-game
.Nd run a Windows game through Proton and WineD3D on OpenGL
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -id Ar id
.Op Fl -prefix Ar directory
.Op Fl -print
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar program Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Ar program
through the x86-64 GNU root's GE-Proton11-12 at
.Pa /opt/proton/proton .
It uses WoW64 and WineD3D's OpenGL renderer with fsync enabled.
Steam is not required.
The program's arguments and exit status pass through Proton.
.Pp
.Fl -id
chooses a decimal game ID.
The default is the inherited
.Ev SteamGameId ,
or 0.
Give each game its own ID or compatibility directory.
.Fl -prefix
chooses that directory; Proton keeps the Wine prefix in its
.Pa pfx
child.
It takes precedence over
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_DATA_PATH .
With neither, the directory is
.Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/rach2/games/ID
or
.Pa $HOME/.local/share/rach2/games/ID .
All directory paths must be absolute.
.Pp
When the compatibility directory has no
.Pa pfx/user.reg ,
.Nm
first makes the prefix: it runs
.Li wineboot -u
through Proton, then sets
.Li VideoMemorySize
under
.Li HKCU\eSoftware\eWine\eDirect3D
to the machine's memory in MiB, the
.Li MemTotal
of
.Pa /proc/meminfo .
The GPUs Rach2 drives draw from system memory, and WineD3D otherwise takes
the size the GL driver reports, which virgl gives as a size no memory has.
It prints
.Dl rach2-game: prefix: made DIR with VideoMemorySize N MiB
on standard error before it starts the program.
An existing prefix keeps its key.
.Pp
.Fl -print
prints the effective settings, one
.Ar NAME=value
per line, without creating directories or starting Proton.
No program is needed in this mode.
.Fl -help
prints usage.
.Fl -
ends option processing.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm
sets these variables for Proton:
.Bl -tag -width STEAM_COMPAT_CLIENT_INSTALL_PATH
.It Ev PROTON_USE_WOW64
1, selecting Wine's WoW64 mode.
.It Ev PROTON_USE_WINED3D
1, selecting WineD3D instead of DXVK and vkd3d-proton.
.It Ev WINE_D3D_CONFIG
.Li renderer=gl ,
selecting OpenGL.
.It Ev PROTON_NO_FSYNC
0; Proton enables fsync and Wine checks the kernel's futex support.
.It Ev SteamGameId , SteamAppId
The chosen game ID.
.It Ev PROTON_LOG
1, enabling Proton's log and DLL load records.
.El
.Pp
.Ev PROTON_LOG_DIR
chooses the log directory; its default is
.Pa logs
in the compatibility directory.
Proton writes
.Pa steam-ID.log
there, replacing the preceding launch's log.
.Pp
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_CLIENT_INSTALL_PATH
is kept when set; otherwise it names
.Pa steam
under the default
.Pa rach2/games
directory.
The launcher creates this directory for Proton without installing Steam.
.Ev DISPLAY
and the desktop session's other variables pass through unchanged.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Usage errors exit with status 2.
A failed
.Li wineboot
or
.Li reg
in a new prefix exits with status 1.
Otherwise the exit status is Proton's.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rach2-game --id 17300 --prefix /data/crysis/compat /data/crysis/Bin64/Crysis.exe -dx9
rach2-game --id 17300 --print
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr innoextract 1 ,
.Xr proton 1 ,
.Xr desktop 7
